## Statement

Over `F=Q(gamma)`, let `A0` be the invertible `4426 x 4426` B89 H11
complement and let `U,W` be the selected G3CV factors. Define

```text
Q = W A0^-1 U.
```

Consider the bordered matrix

```text
B = [ A0  U ]
    [ W   0 ].
```

Since `A0` is invertible, exact Schur elimination gives

```text
rank_F(B) = 4426 + rank_F(Q).
```

The exact polynomial support of `B` has a maximum bipartite matching of size
`5136`. An explicit vertex cover of the same size certifies maximality.
Consequently

```text
rank_F(Q) <= 5136 - 4426 = 710.
```

At the good reduction `(21817,gamma-5)`, the G3CW matrix `Q` has a nonzero
`710 x 710` minor, with determinant `17520`. Reduction cannot increase rank,
so

```text
rank_F(Q) >= 710.
```

The two bounds meet:

```text
rank_Q(gamma)(W A0^-1 U) = 710.
```

## Second Reduction

The emitted nonzero minor selects rows `R` and columns `C`. Set

```text
U_Q = Q[:,C],
T_Q = Q[R,C],
W_Q = Q[R,:].
```

Then, exactly over `Q(gamma)`,

```text
Q = U_Q T_Q^-1 W_Q.
```

Therefore the first reduced equation

```text
